Game Design Document: Area
1. Game Overview
Title: Area
Genre: Stylized FPS / Tactical Arena / Battle Royale
Platform: PC only
Perspective: First-Person
Player Count: 5–10 players (2 teams max 10 per team)
Art Style: Low-poly, stylized, minimalist. Hexagon motif in gameplay and UI.
Game Feel: Fortnite-style building/movement freedom + Halo weapon pickup + Call-of-Duty-like gun combat finesse
Premise:
Players are dropped into a dome arena without weapons and must find them on the map. Traditional “kills” are modified: players have life shards in their home base, meaning defeating someone requires stealing and returning their shard. Only teammates can revive them.
2. Core Mechanics
2.1 Movement & Combat
Walk, sprint, jump, crouch
Build low-poly structures (ramps, walls, floors) for cover or height advantage
Weapons:
Pistol
Assault Rifle
Shotgun
Sniper
Special-grade (rare spawns at designated drop points)
Melee: Fist, Knife (body damage system: head > body > limbs)
Weapon pickups spawn at fixed or randomized locations (like Halo)
2.2 Life Shard System
Each player has a life shard in their team’s home base
Collecting an opponent’s shard and returning it to your base disintegrates the opposing player immediately
Only the shard owner’s teammate can return it to revive them
Encourages strategy and teamwork over raw killing
2.3 Perks / Chance Blocks
Hexagon-themed blocks scattered on the map or behind walls
Activated using action button → random perk
Examples:
Grow 3x larger
Infinite ammo
Increased run speed (limited time)
Perks randomized each round
Encourages dynamic, unpredictable gameplay
3. Arena & Map Design
3.1 Standard Dome Arena
Medium-sized, closed dome
Strategic weapon spawns
Team bases with life shards clearly marked
Low-poly terrain: ramps, walls, floors (placeholders or custom assets)
3.2 Battle Royale Arena (Optional/Advanced)
Large map, open environment
Safe zone shrinks over time (classic Battle Royale style)
Last team or player alive wins
Weapon/perk drops scattered across the map
3.3 Visual Style
Minimalist, low-poly design
Hexagons as the recurring theme:
Perk blocks
Some terrain patterns
UI elements
Player models: simple, gender-based variations only
Future modding support possible for skins or map variations
4. Game Loop
Players drop into arena (empty-handed or starting weapon)
Players search for weapons and build for cover
Combat occurs to steal life shards and defend own shard
Activate perks via chance blocks for tactical advantage
Teammates can revive shard-less players
Round ends when all opponents’ shards are captured OR in Battle Royale mode, last player/team standing
5. Combat Mechanics & Damage
Headshot → highest damage
Body → medium
Limbs → low
Melee damage: fists/knife for close combat
Firearms balanced for low-to-mid combat intensity
Special weapons less frequent → higher impact
6. Spawn & Respawn
Players spawn at home base initially
Weapon pickups scattered in arena
Life shard system replaces traditional respawn:
No shard → cannot play until revived by teammate
Encourages coordination
7. Progression & Scoring
No leaderboard for now
Future: XP, cosmetic unlocks, skins, or mod support possible
8. Game Feel / Key Design Goals
Stylized but competitive
Fast, strategic gameplay — not purely shooting
Hexagon motif visible in perks, map, and UI
Low-poly aesthetic keeps focus on gameplay mechanics
Tactical teamwork is rewarded over lone-wolf kills
9. Assets & Placeholders
Ramps, walls, floors — can be replaced with final assets later
Weapon models: basic placeholders
Perk blocks: hexagonal objects with interaction triggers
Low-poly environment: keeps game performant and visually cohesive
10. Future Expansion Ideas
Leaderboards, stats tracking
Cosmetic skins / modding support
Advanced Battle Royale arena
Additional weapons, vehicles, or special-grade guns
Team emblems / shard customization
